  "dog_detail": "No breed ban in force in Mumbai or Maharashtra. The March 2024 central circular on 23 breeds (incl. pit bull, AmStaff, SBT and mixes) was quashed by the Karnataka and Delhi High Courts; in the Bombay High Court PIL the Union told the court it is 'not acting on the circular' and has opened public consultation, and Maharashtra confirmed no state order was issued on its basis. Pressure is rising: after a July 2025 pit bull attack on a boy in Mumbai, PETA India formally asked Maharashtra to ban nine breeds including pit bulls and XL Bullies, and neighbouring Goa and Jharkhand enacted bans in 2025. BMC pet licences (MMC Act s.191B) are mandatory and now online.",
  "dog_mix_rule": "No legal identification today; the quashed circular would have covered mixes. Any future Maharashtra or re-issued central rule would almost certainly name 'pit bull and mixes' and could arrive with little notice.",
  "dog_import": "Mumbai (BOM) is one of the six AQCS entry airports. Advance NOC from AQCS Mumbai (INR 1,000 fee, apply 7+ working days ahead) under transfer-of-residence (2+ years abroad, max 2 pets); ISO microchip; rabies within 12 months; USDA-endorsed health certificate on the Indian format; no titre; clearance at the Quarantine Station on arrival, normally same-day with no quarantine. Air India nonstop from the US accepts dogs as cargo (no bully-breed exclusion listed).",
